Upgrade procedure for less

Source: https://greenwoodsoftware.com/less/less-VERSION.tar.gz

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download and extract the official less-VERSION.tar.gz release archive.
2. Import it on vendor/less/dist, retaining the complete upstream release.
3. Merge it into master with:

       git subtree merge -P contrib/less vendor/less/dist

4. Keep the master-only files and compatibility changes described below.

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  - 886d52f19ea3e264811d0a93fce22af07fc0e6aa: Apply less is more
    patches from FreeBSD.  Preserve less-is-more behavior in command.c,
    forwback.c, main.c, pattern.h, and signal.c.  The patches are applied
    around command-mode search modifiers (command.c mca_search_char: '*'
    and '@' are ignored when less_is_more), forward-screen handling
    (forwback.c forw(): no need_home and squish on every screen when
    less_is_more), option parsing and terminal initialization (main.c:
    "more" implies scan_option("-fG"), isoptstring() rejects '+' options,
    no_init = TRUE, and the "terminal is not fully functional" warning is
    suppressed), POSIX basic regular expressions (pattern.h REGCOMP_FLAG
    is 0 when less_is_more), and interrupt handling (signal.c).

  - 0828cc62cd5d05bba93fb2ea29c35922e7febd9f: Port the less-is-more
    changes to less 704.  In less.h, retain the HAVE_WCTYPE_H guard and
    wctype.h include; HAVE_WCTYPE is enabled by usr.bin/less/defines.h.

  - less 710 import: upstream now declares less_is_more itself as
    "lbool" (main.c, option.c, prompt.c).  The local extern declarations
    added by the patches above (command.c, forwback.c, pattern.h,
    signal.c) must use "extern lbool less_is_more;" to match.

Notes:

  - master excludes upstream configuration files, non-Unix makefiles,
    generated manual pages (*.man), install helpers, and the lesstest
    directory.  Keep those exclusions after each subtree merge (resolve
    the modify/delete conflicts with git rm).
  - Use the Less License included in LICENSE; COPYING is intentionally
    excluded from the master subtree.
  - less 710 removed lesskey.c and the lesskey(1) program; lesskey files
    are compiled by less itself via lesskey_parse.c.  usr.bin/lesskey was
    removed and lesskey(5) (lesskey.nro) is now installed from
    usr.bin/less.  New sources lmsg.c/lmsg.h and the lessmsg* message
    tables must be kept; lmsg.c is listed in usr.bin/less/Makefile.
  - usr.bin/less/defines.h is maintained by hand (no configure run);
    compare it against upstream defines.h.in after each import.  It keeps
    MidnightBSD's /etc/lesskey and /etc/syslesskey paths and HAVE_WCTYPE.
